{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers","id":1300646,"title":"Captain Marvel [Spoilers]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-28T13:10:39-07:00","id":1300646,"title":"Captain Marvel [Spoilers]","content":"So, how much is Captain Marvel an Exalted story?<br /> <br /> A gigantic empire is hunting down an army of shapeshifting refugees of their continual wars, using a captured and mind wiped glowing golden hero, who learns of this evil and defects to the side of the shapeshifters, single handedly taking out an imperial armada in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T13:21:25-07:00","id":1300648,"title":"","content":"Well, the big thing is that the Skrull are in a lot worse shape than the Lunars and are fleeing rather than trying to overthrow the Kree Empire, but . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T13:31:06-07:00","id":1300651,"title":"","content":"Well, she does very clearly have a Solar anima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T13:36:47-07:00","id":1300655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300648#post1300648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the big thing is that the Skrull are in a lot worse shape than the Lunars and are fleeing rather than trying to overthrow the Kree Empire, but . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, also one Lunar would almost never lose to a single DB in a fight, but who knows, maybe there\u2019s an Empire of the Bear equivalent out there by the time of Avengers.<br /> <br /> Then again the Skrulls ultimate goal also isn\u2019t to bring down the Kree I don\u2019t think, but again maybe with a power base that would change. It certainly is Captain Marvel\u2019s plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T19:46:31-07:00","id":1300734,"title":"","content":"The Solar in this metaphor isn't being hunted down by the empire until like the last third of the movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T20:41:54-07:00","id":1300745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300734#post1300734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar in this metaphor isn't being hunted down by the empire until like the last third of the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can imagine some Dragon-Bloods trying to take advantage of an amnesiac Dawn by pointing her at their enemies. It'd have to be a hushed-up thing that flew in the face of Immaculate dogma rather than her being a state-sponsored champion, but it's the kind of thing that could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:21:51-07:00","id":1300751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300745#post1300745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One can imagine some Dragon-Bloods trying to take advantage of an amnesiac Dawn by pointing her at their enemies. It'd have to be a hushed-up thing that flew in the face of Immaculate dogma rather than her being a state-sponsored champion, but it's the kind of thing that could happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually played in a game that did exactly that. Having a pet solar that can destroy an entire army solo with one arm tied behind her back was too valuable to pass up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T10:05:35-07:00","id":1300867,"title":"","content":"I also saw some Gold Faction trying to control a young Solar and it blowing up in their face spectacularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:08:08-07:00","id":1300939,"title":"","content":"I've heard some conflicting things.<br /> <br /> Like, plot and continuity conflicts.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Tesseract, which Howard Stark fished out of the ocean and gave to SHIELD, somehow got stolen by a Kree woman posing as a human woman. Does Coulson or Fury ever talk about looking for that thing? It's pretty important. They've still got Dr. Zola around, as well as samples of the weapons he made with the thing. They know how dangerous it is.<br /> <br /> This Kree woman had a super-stealthy spaceship in orbit around Earth, equipped with a better lab than anything on Earth, but the Kree woman is designing and testing the light-speed engine as a human woman on Earth. Which would make sense if she couldn't steal the Tesseract and had to remain undercover to conduct her experiments, but she clearly did steal the cube and take it to her orbiting lab, so why did she go back?<br /> <br /> When the Kree man showed up, he killed the Kree woman, and he saw Carol Danvers destroy the light-speed engine. He takes her back to his planet because the power she absorbed made her into a useful novelty... but the Kree don't look for the orbiting lab or the Tesseract?<br /> <br /> The Skrull capture Carol and look through her memories to find where she came from so they can find other Skrulls who are hidden on the orbiting space lab though they say they're looking for the engine for some reason. (I suppose there's a reason why the Skrulls in the lab didn't let their relatives know where they were going to be? Did the Kree lady kidnap them or something? What were they doing for all the time the Kree woman was dead?)<br /> <br /> The Kree follow Carol back to Earth to find the light-speed engine that the Kree man watched get destroyed right before his eyes? And he doesn't even know the Tesseract was involved? Didn't suspect the presence of the orbiting space lab?<br /> <br /> SHIELD only begins using the Tesseract to make weapons after Thor arrives, even though SHIELD knew about powers like Carol Danvers, the shape-shifting Skrull, the war-mongering Kree, and thus the possibility of even worse threats out there?<br /> <br /> Black Widow and Hawkeye are completely unprepared for Loki and his space-invader army in The Avengers despite the events of Captain Marvel as SHIELD's warning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T17:02:11-07:00","id":1300980,"title":"","content":"Okay, I only saw the movie once, so . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tesseract, which Howard Stark fished out of the ocean and gave to SHIELD, somehow got stolen by a Kree woman posing as a human woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>When, posing as a human woman, she joined the SHIELD/NASA/Air Force joint project trying to harness the Tesseract as an energy source, yes. (Since Howard Stark was still alive in 1989 [the year the lightspeed engine was destroyed], it's even possible that he knew what she was and actually <i>gave</i> the thing to Mar-Vell.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Coulson or Fury ever talk about looking for that thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fury in the movie is shown to be only a level 3 SHIELD agent; Coulson is junior to Fury. Compartmentalization of dangerous information is not just sensible, it's established SHIELD practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Kree woman had a super-stealthy spaceship in orbit around Earth, equipped with a better lab than anything on Earth, but the Kree woman is designing and testing the light-speed engine as a human woman on Earth. Which would make sense if she couldn't steal the Tesseract and had to remain undercover to conduct her experiments, but she clearly did steal the cube and take it to her orbiting lab, so why did she go back?</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that she needed no Earth resources, human or otherwise, to develop the engine or ship after stealing the Tesseract. No matter how nice the lab is on her ship, this is hardly a given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Kree man showed up, he killed the Kree woman, and he saw Carol Danvers destroy the light-speed engine. He takes her back to his planet because the power she absorbed made her into a useful novelty... but the Kree don't look for the orbiting lab or the Tesseract?</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that the Kree knew the Tesseract was part of the engine project and was not in the engine when it was destroyed. There is no reason to make either of those assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose there's a reason why the Skrulls in the lab didn't let their relatives know where they were going to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the obvious one would be that if you let someone who's out fighting the Kree know where your hidden refuge for non-combatants is, there's a decent chance that he'll be captured, fed to the Supreme Intelligence to be forced to disgorge the location, and lead the Kree right to Mar-Vell/the refugees/the lightspeed engine. Compartmentalization of dangerous information is just sensible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kree follow Carol back to Earth to find the light-speed engine that the Kree man watched get destroyed right before his eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they follow Vers back to Earth to find Vers and maybe whatever the Skrulls are interested in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SHIELD only begins using the Tesseract to make weapons after Thor arrives, even though SHIELD knew about powers like Carol Danvers, the shape-shifting Skrull, the war-mongering Kree, and thus the possibility of even worse threats out there?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've got Carol Danvers on pager.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Widow and Hawkeye are completely unprepared for Loki and his space-invader army in The Avengers despite the events of Captain Marvel as SHIELD's warning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Compartmentalization of dangerous information is established SHIELD practice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T18:17:32-07:00","id":1300990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300980#post1300980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When, posing as a human woman, she joined the SHIELD/NASA/Air Force joint project trying to harness the Tesseract as an energy source, yes. (Since Howard Stark was still alive in 1989 [the year the lightspeed engine was destroyed], it's even possible that he knew what she was and actually <i>gave</i> the thing to Mar-Vell.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The cube really isn't Stark's to give to anyone, since the USA would have declared it government property the moment they got their hands on it. And that's assuming he would give it to an alien he barely knows.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, they know mere humans can figure the Tesseract out, because that's what Zola already did. And they still have Zola in custody, working for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fury in the movie is shown to be only a level 3 SHIELD agent; Coulson is junior to Fury. Compartmentalization of dangerous information is not just sensible, it's established SHIELD practice. </div> </div> </div>Granted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This assumes that she needed no Earth resources, human or otherwise, to develop the engine or ship after stealing the Tesseract. No matter how nice the lab is on her ship, this is hardly a given. </div> </div> </div>If Howard Stark or any other human scientist, like Zola, was helping her, and extended enough trust to let her take the cube to her spaceship, perhaps she might have repaid them with enough trust to take them with her onto her spaceship? Together with whatever material resources Howard could buy or requisition from SHIELD.<br /> <br /> Actually, why was SHE on Earth and not the shapeshifters she had with her? Why were the shapeshifters confined to the orbiting spaceship?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This assumes that the Kree knew the Tesseract was part of the engine project and was not in the engine when it was destroyed. There is no reason to make either of those assumptions. </div> </div> </div>That leaves aside the space-ship. Mar-Vell had to have gotten to Earth somehow, so she must have had a ship around somewhere, and I don't think the Kree would want to risk humans finding their technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, the obvious one would be that if you let someone who's out fighting the Kree know where your hidden refuge for non-combatants is, there's a decent chance that he'll be captured, fed to the Supreme Intelligence to be forced to disgorge the location, and lead the Kree right to Mar-Vell/the refugees/the lightspeed engine. Compartmentalization of dangerous information is just sensible. </div> </div> </div>Granted.<br /> <br /> But then, why did the Skrulls go looking for them? Did they learn that Mar-Vell had died? If their spies were able to determine that, it's a little odd that they didn't discover where Mar-Vell was killed at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe they follow Vers back to Earth to find Vers and maybe whatever the Skrulls are interested in. </div> </div> </div>Sounds plausible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They've got Carol Danvers on pager. </div> </div> </div>Did Fury happen to misplace that pager for every previous Avengers movie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T19:24:06-07:00","id":1301005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SHIELD only begins using the Tesseract to make weapons after Thor arrives</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they? It\u2019s been years but I don\u2019t recall the start date of that program being mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300990#post1300990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Fury happen to misplace that pager for every previous Avengers movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything\u2019s always been over and done way faster than she could have been there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 03-29-2019, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T19:39:17-07:00","id":1301006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300990#post1300990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Fury happen to misplace that pager for every previous Avengers movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly his plan has been to use it only after the Avengers failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T19:57:39-07:00","id":1301009,"title":"","content":"Let's break down the incidents in the Avengers movies.<br /> <br /> <i>Avengers</i> - Loki's attack on NYC and the Avengers' defeat of it takes only slightly more time overall than the city's overall response time to an emergency 911 call. For all we know, he <i>did</i> page her, and had to sheepishly admit to her afterward that Tony and the others already took care of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Avengers 2 - Avenge Harder</i> - Ultron's &quot;Age&quot; is over in mere days, and his whole &quot;slam a city into the Earth&quot; business is resolved from start to finish in less time than it takes for me to cook a nice dinner for just myself.<br /> <br /> <i>Avengers 3 - Thanos Directly Caused More People to Starve via His Devastation of Supply Chains Than Would Ever Have From 'Using Up Resources' (Hey, You Know What's a Resource? Life Itself, and You Just Took Out Half of It)</i> - S.H.I.E.L.D. doesn't have assets in Wakanda, so all they saw was a brief alien attack that was resolved by superheroes on the scene in less time than it takes to get a pizza delivered, and then some unspecified time later, a guy snaps his fingers and half of everyone is dead.<br /> <br /> Why not ask why she didn't get called on to stop every mass tragedy between her debut and now? The answer is, they happen too fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-01-2019, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T21:53:55-07:00","id":1301029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300990#post1300990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Fury happen to misplace that pager for every previous Avengers movie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of God is that he used it in the first Avengers movie, but that the situation was resolved by the Avengers before she arrived.<br /> <br /> For the third Avengers movie, he used it on-screen, as seen in the post-credits scene. And in the mid-credits scene in Captain Marvel, we see her arrive in response and ask where Fury is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":"sentence deleted. 03-30-2019, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T22:39:51-07:00","id":1301037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard some conflicting things.<br /> <br /> Like, plot and continuity conflicts.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Tesseract, which Howard Stark fished out of the ocean and gave to SHIELD, somehow got stolen by a Kree woman posing as a human woman. Does Coulson or Fury ever talk about looking for that thing? It's pretty important. They've still got Dr. Zola around, as well as samples of the weapons he made with the thing. They know how dangerous it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would relatively new field agents (one a rookie, the other a CIA transfer), know anything about one of SHIELD\u2019s most highly classified secrets? We don\u2019t know how it ended up in Mar Vel\u2019s possession, but as she got it 40 years after Howard found it, I don\u2019t see a continuity conflict, just an untold story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Kree woman had a super-stealthy spaceship in orbit around Earth, equipped with a better lab than anything on Earth, but the Kree woman is designing and testing the light-speed engine as a human woman on Earth. Which would make sense if she couldn't steal the Tesseract and had to remain undercover to conduct her experiments, but she clearly did steal the cube and take it to her orbiting lab, so why did she go back? </div> </div> </div>Because she doesn\u2019t have the construction infrastructure to build what she needs on her ship, so she goes back and forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Kree man showed up, he killed the Kree woman, and he saw Carol Danvers destroy the light-speed engine. He takes her back to his planet because the power she absorbed made her into a useful novelty... but the Kree don't look for the orbiting lab or the Tesseract? </div> </div> </div>They didn\u2019t know nearly as much about the tesseract as the Skrull who were working with Mar Vel did. Yon Rog thought the engine was the power source he was looking for, so now it was Carol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Skrull capture Carol and look through her memories to find where she came from so they can find other Skrulls who are hidden on the orbiting space lab though they say they're looking for the engine for some reason. (I suppose there's a reason why the Skrulls in the lab didn't let their relatives know where they were going to be? Did the Kree lady kidnap them or something? What were they doing for all the time the Kree woman was dead?) </div> </div> </div>Refugee families are often separated where some get left behind waiting for information or passage to reunite later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Kree follow Carol back to Earth to find the light-speed engine that the Kree man watched get destroyed right before his eyes? And he doesn't even know the Tesseract was involved? Didn't suspect the presence of the orbiting space lab? </div> </div> </div>They thought the engine was all there was, then thanks to the Skrull efforts they discovered the existence of the lab and the separate power source. I don\u2019t get why this confused anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SHIELD only begins using the Tesseract to make weapons after Thor arrives, even though SHIELD knew about powers like Carol Danvers, the shape-shifting Skrull, the war-mongering Kree, and thus the possibility of even worse threats out there? </div> </div> </div>They didn\u2019t start that project after Thor, they just recruited Skarsgaard then. ShIELD has known about the weapon powering potential of the Tesseract since the 40s. The employed Zola for Christ\u2019s sake! Presumably Peggy stopped something like \u201cPhase 2\u201d until she was forced out. Which would chronologically line up with Mar Vel getting the Tesseract. Perhaps Peggy knew her and gave it to her to keep it out of the hands of the shadowy forces in SHIELD she suspected but could not identify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Black Widow and Hawkeye are completely unprepared for Loki and his space-invader army in The Avengers despite the events of Captain Marvel as SHIELD's warning? </div> </div> </div>SHIELD keeps secrets from its own agents!? What a shocking revelation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-30-2019, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T17:54:19-07:00","id":1301195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1300939#post1300939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard some conflicting things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that some of these issues are resolved by watching the movie.<br /> <br /> Either in terms of the arrangement in context addressing some concerns, or else the overall tone and texture making them feel as though they matter a lot less.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T18:00:42-07:00","id":1301196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1301029#post1301029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word of God is that he used it in the first Avengers movie, but that the situation was resolved by the Avengers before she arrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing it\u2019s the kind that can send texts to let her know \u201cNever mind we won,\u201d else that would have been <i>really</i> awkward. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T18:51:40-07:00","id":1301201,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to ignore the word of God on that and go with my own headcanon that Calling Carol was Fury\u2019s backup plan if the Avengers and New York fell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T19:06:28-07:00","id":1301202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300646-captain-marvel-spoilers?p=1301201#post1301201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m going to ignore the word of God on that and go with my own headcanon that Calling Carol was Fury\u2019s backup plan if the Avengers and New York fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the attack on New York was over in only slightly longer than real-life NYC's 911 response time, and she has to <i>get there</i>. Calling her as it's happening isn't a bad move; if he waited until the Avengers were defeated to call her pager, a second city may very well have destroyed while Nick Fury dicked around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2019, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}